-- FAILING (Bug I). An effect-typed conditional (the @throw makes it effectful)
-- whose OTHER arm is itself a value-producing conditional (`? b > 0 = 1 : 2`,
-- arms are plain values, so it yields a value, not a thunk). The Bug C fix
-- wraps LEAF value arms (Int/Str/Tuple/...) in a thunk to match the @throw
-- arm's thunk representation, but a nested value-CONDITIONAL arm is neither a
-- leaf value nor thunk-valued, so it stays unwrapped and inconsistent with its
-- @throw sibling. Realized in C++ this is a compile error (a value assigned to
-- a std::function); realized in Python it is `'int' object is not callable` at
-- runtime. A no-@throw sibling (`? a>0 = 9 : (? b>0 = 1 : 2)`) works. This file
-- must build once the arm-thunking recurses into value-conditional arms.
module main (nv)

import root-py
import root-cpp

nv :: Int -> Int -> <Err> Int
nv a b =
  ? a > 0 = @throw "outer"
  : (? b > 0 = 1 : 2)
